Marginal Improvement Reciprocity License, Version 1.0 ("MIRL-1.0")

Copyright (c) 2026 R. Michael Glover

This is a source-available license, not an Open Source Initiative-approved
open-source license. Its purpose is to permit learning, sharing, and genuine
improvement while preventing extraction of capital from the Work.

1. Definitions

"Work" means the software, documentation, writing, art, data, and other
material distributed with this license, except material identified as being
under another license or owned by someone else.

"Source" means the preferred form for studying and making changes, including
the scripts, build instructions, and corresponding assets reasonably needed
to reproduce a distributed or publicly performed version.

"Modification" means any adaptation, derivative work, or other change to the
Work.

"Significant Marginal Improvement" means a good-faith, non-trivial
Modification that produces a demonstrable improvement over the version used.
It must materially improve at least one relevant quality—such as capability,
correctness, accessibility, safety, privacy, resource efficiency,
maintainability, documentation, pedagogy, or artistic expression—and must not
obtain that improvement chiefly by degrading another relevant quality. Merely
renaming, rebranding, repackaging, changing prices, adding advertising,
removing attribution, or making cosmetic changes is not sufficient.

"Independent Worker" means one natural person acting as a sole proprietor or
otherwise selling that person's own labor, without employees, investors,
shareholders, partners who share profits, or a business entity other than a
single-member disregarded entity wholly owned and controlled by that person.
Independent consultants, freelancers, and educators may qualify. A worker
does not cease to qualify solely because a client reports payments on a U.S.
Form 1099 or a comparable form.

"Commercial Use" means use primarily intended for commercial advantage or
monetary compensation, whether direct or indirect.

"Capital Return" means revenue or economic benefit based primarily on
ownership rather than the natural person's own labor. It includes dividends,
profit distributions to investors or passive owners, interest derived from
the Work, royalties for access to the Work or a Modification, equity value or
fundraising value attributed to them, sale of a business or other capital
asset whose value materially includes them, and rent-seeking or financialized
claims against them. Ordinary fees paid directly for an Independent Worker's
personal consulting, freelance, or educational labor are not Capital Return.

"Trust of Trusts" means the stewardship body originally founded and led by
R. Michael Glover to oversee commercial uses of the Work. Until a separate
legal trust or other stewardship entity is publicly designated by R. Michael
Glover in this repository, "Trust of Trusts" means R. Michael Glover acting as
the initial steward. A successor has authority under this license only after a
public, dated designation is added to the repository by the then-authorized
steward. Its reviewing board is the Board of Trustees of Trustees described in
the stewardship charter distributed with the Work. Board service is limited to
engineers who voluntarily accept a written zero-compensation service agreement;
no person or employer is appointed or bound merely by being named or eligible.

"Stewardship Approval" means specific, prior, express written permission from
the Trust of Trusts for the particular person, version, improvement, scope,
clients or audience, compensation model, and time period proposed. Silence,
source availability, acceptance of a contribution, or approval of a different
use is not Stewardship Approval.

2. Noncommercial permission

Subject to this license, the Licensor grants everyone a worldwide,
non-exclusive, royalty-free, non-sublicensable copyright license to use, study,
copy, modify, publicly perform, publicly display, and distribute the Work and
Modifications for purposes that are not Commercial Use.

3. Limited commercial permission for independent labor

Commercial Use is permitted only when all of the following are true:

a. The Trust of Trusts has reviewed the proposed use and granted Stewardship
   Approval before any offer, sale, invoice, paid instruction, paid advice,
   monetized deployment, or other money-making activity begins;
b. Every person receiving monetary compensation from the use is an
   Independent Worker, and the compensation is for that person's own labor;
c. Before requesting Stewardship Approval and before offering or providing the
   commercial product or service, that
   Independent Worker creates a Significant Marginal Improvement;
d. The complete Source of the Significant Marginal Improvement is made
   publicly available, without charge, in a durable and readily accessible
   repository under this same license no later than the first commercial use;
e. The public Source includes a clear description and reasonable evidence of
   the claimed improvement, instructions sufficient to reproduce or evaluate
   it, attribution to this Work, and a copy of this license; and
f. No person or entity receives, seeks, promises, collateralizes, or
   accumulates a Capital Return from the Work or any Modification.

The Trust of Trusts may approve or decline a request in its stewardship
judgment and may condition approval on reporting and verification consistent
with this license. Creating or publishing an improvement does not create a
right to earn money. Stewardship Approval is always required and does not
waive any other condition.

For clarity, a company, partnership, nonprofit organization, government body,
investment fund, employer, platform acting as principal, or other organization
may not exercise the commercial permission in this section. It may hire an
Independent Worker for that worker's personal labor only if the organization
itself does not copy, deploy, distribute, publicly perform, or otherwise use
the Work or a Modification for Commercial Use. No artificial division of an
organization or transaction may be used to evade this section.

4. Sharing and public performance

Any distribution of a Modification, and any public performance of a modified
version over a computer network, must include or conspicuously link to its
complete Source and license the Modification as a whole under this same
license. You must preserve copyright, attribution, license, and third-party
notices. You must state that you changed the Work and identify the date of the
change. You may not impose terms or technological measures that restrict a
recipient's exercise of the permissions this license grants.

Distribution of an unmodified copy is permitted under section 2, but charging
for the copy or access to it is Commercial Use and requires full compliance
with section 3, including a separate Significant Marginal Improvement.

5. No trademark or endorsement rights

This license grants no rights in names, trademarks, service marks, or trade
dress, and does not permit you to imply endorsement by the Licensor.

6. Patents

The Licensor grants you a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive patent
license under patent claims the Licensor can license that are necessarily
infringed by your permitted use of the Work. If you or an organization you
control initiate patent litigation alleging that the Work or a Modification
infringes a patent, all patent rights granted to you by this section terminate.

7. Compliance and termination

Your rights terminate automatically if you fail to comply. They reinstate
automatically if you cure the violation within 30 days after first learning
of it, provided this is your first violation. Otherwise, reinstatement
requires the Licensor's express written permission. Sections 5, 8, and 9
survive termination.

