11. Additional permission and stewardship decisions

The Licensor may grant additional permission in writing. Only the Trust of
Trusts may grant Stewardship Approval. Additional permission or Stewardship
Approval for one person, use, or version does not change this license for
anyone else. The Trust of Trusts may publish nonbinding procedures and review
criteria, but may not use them to eliminate the express conditions in section
3 without issuing a new license version from the copyright owner.

The stewardship charter is explanatory governance unless incorporated into a
signed legal instrument. If it conflicts with this license, this license
controls the permissions to use the Work.

12. Interpretation

If a provision is unenforceable, it will be reformed only as much as necessary
to make it enforceable, and the remainder stays effective. Headings and the
plain-language summary distributed with the Work are explanatory only; these
terms control. This license creates conditions on the copyright and patent
permissions granted here and does not waive limitations or exceptions supplied
by applicable law.

This license governs use of the protected Work; it does not claim ownership of
general knowledge, abstract ideas, facts, skills, or expertise that copyright
and patent law leave free for others to use.
